-- The @nlg written above a rule is that rule's, whatever comes before it. The
-- CONSIDERs that a rule written as clauses is lowered to hold names that the
-- parser made up, which have no place in the file; they used to take the
-- @nlg of the rule after the group, so that it was never used (refutation of
-- legalese/l4-ide#545's review, round 4). Each rule below is rendered with
-- its own, as its twin written as one definition is.
DECLARE Colour IS ONE OF Red, Green

-- A rule with no GIVEN after a group.
GIVEN c IS A Colour
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE one Red IS 1
DECIDE one Green IS 2
@nlg the second rule
DECIDE two IS 1

-- A group with no GIVEN after a group.
GIVEN c IS A Colour
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE three Red IS 1
DECIDE three Green IS 2
@nlg the fourth rule
DECIDE four Red IS 1
DECIDE four Green IS 2

-- A group with a GIVEN after a group, whose @nlg is above its first clause.
GIVEN c IS A Colour
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE five Red IS 1
DECIDE five Green IS 2
GIVEN c IS A Colour
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the sixth rule, for %c%
DECIDE six Red IS 1
DECIDE six Green IS 2

#EVAL one Green
#EVAL two
#EVAL three Green
#EVAL four Green
#EVAL five Green
#EVAL six Green
